[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-24361"] :question/problem "Find the exact value of $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={7.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {7.5}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x={15}^{∘},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-327771/field-1/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "05d612ff-c79f-57e5-8848-f245950c16b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327771/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "36e1c06e-02b3-5eb3-bb38-89c94e3dba9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327771/field-1/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer-field/choices ["q-327771/field-1/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327771" :question/id #uuid "92adad31-0676-5e5c-b234-81f262965d25" :question/math-academy-id "q-327771" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}.$\n\n$4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={15}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327771/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327771"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
